# SCLS (Scientific Core Library Stack)

> SCLS builds and packages a consistent stack of scientific libraries ({{ seo_package_names | join(', ') }}) for Linux and macOS. Every library in a flavor is built with the same compiler, MPI (Open MPI), BLAS/LAPACK and install prefix, so PETSc, MUMPS, STRUMPACK, SuperLU, Ipopt and HDF5 work together without manual compilation. Binary RPM repositories serve Enterprise Linux 9 and 10 and Amazon Linux 2023; binary DEB repositories serve Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and 26.04 LTS; macOS and other Unix systems build from source. Developed at Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, licensed BSD-3-Clause-LBNL.

## Flavors

A flavor fixes compiler, math backend, MPI and install prefix for the whole stack. Each public flavor installs into /opt/scls/<flavor>:

