## Install on Enterprise Linux 9 / 10 or Amazon Linux 2023

```
# Enterprise Linux 9:
sudo dnf install https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/el9/x86_64/Packages/scls-release-{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ scls_release_rpm_release }}.el9.noarch.rpm
# Enterprise Linux 10:
sudo dnf install https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/el10/x86_64/Packages/scls-release-{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ scls_release_rpm_release }}.el10.noarch.rpm
# Amazon Linux 2023:
sudo dnf install https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/amzn2023/x86_64/Packages/scls-release-{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ scls_release_rpm_release }}.amzn2023.noarch.rpm

sudo dnf install scls-<flavor>
source /opt/scls/<flavor>/share/scls/activate
```

## Install on Ubuntu 24.04 or 26.04

```
# Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute):
wget https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/ubuntu/resolute/pool/main/s/scls-archive-keyring/scls-archive-keyring_{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ keyring_release['resolute'] }}_all.deb
sudo apt install ./scls-archive-keyring_{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ keyring_release['resolute'] }}_all.deb
# Ubuntu 24.04 (noble):
wget https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/ubuntu/noble/pool/main/s/scls-archive-keyring/scls-archive-keyring_{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ keyring_release['noble'] }}_all.deb
sudo apt install ./scls-archive-keyring_{{ scls_release_pkg_version }}-{{ keyring_release['noble'] }}_all.deb

sudo apt update
sudo apt install scls-<flavor>
source /opt/scls/<flavor>/share/scls/activate
```

## Build from source (macOS, other Unix)

```
git clone https://github.com/cmesse/scls.git
cd scls
echo "flavor: macos" > flavor.conf    # "flavor: gcc" on Linux
./scls build all
source /opt/scls/share/scls/activate  # macOS; /opt/scls/<flavor>/share/scls/activate on Linux
```

## Use the stack

```
source /opt/scls/gcc/share/scls/activate
mpicc myapp.c -o myapp $(pkg-config --cflags --libs petsc)
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$SCLS"
```

Activation sets PATH, PKG_CONFIG_PATH, CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH, SCLS and SCLS_FLAVOR, plus PETSC_DIR, SLEPC_DIR and MPI_HOME when installed. LD_LIBRARY_PATH is not modified; libraries use rpaths.

## Ipopt and HSL

Ipopt uses the MPI build of MUMPS (the default linear_solver) and SPRAL's SSIDS on every flavor, plus MKL Pardiso on the MKL flavors. SSIDS needs OMP_CANCELLATION=TRUE. The proprietary HSL solvers are not shipped; `./scls build hsl` and `./scls install hsl` build a user-supplied Coin-HSL tarball into a library the packaged Ipopt loads at runtime.

